  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug: integer ranges with `clamp=True` and an open bound now return a value inside the range.\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/click/types.py:754`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Before, it stepped away from the range, so `-5` with `min=0, min_open=True` came back as `-1`. It now comes back as `1`.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`: an open minimum turns `-5` into `1`, and an open maximum turns `9` into `4`.\n\nThe full run of `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py` gave 71 passed, 2 skipped. A separate run of just the range tests (21 passed) confirmed the new cases are included and pass.\n\nThe changes are not committed yet.",
